WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.930
Wire a crucible of solid lead two
bromide into a circuit with a bulb.

2
00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.490
Switch on the supply.

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.530
The bulb stays dark.

4
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.750
Now heat the crucible
until the solid melts.

5
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.570
The bulb lights up.

6
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.430
Why does a bulb light only once
solid lead two bromide has melted?

7
00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.130
In this mission, you'll
meet the electrolytic cell,

8
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.830
and compare it with a
voltaic cell, side by side.

9
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.830
You'll predict the products at each
electrode when a molten salt is electrolysed.

10
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:35.550
Your mission: explain why molten lead two
bromide conducts, but the solid doesn't.
